(597571, 60852, 16075, '<td valign="top">I am absolutely shocked that this picture did not place higher.  I gave it a 10 and I still think it should have been a ribbon winner.  You can feel the coarse texture of the fur, the grainy texture of the skin around rim of the eye and even the hair stuck on the eyeball makes me blink thinking about how that must feel.  I think you were robbed!</td>', 'I am absolutely shocked that this picture did not place higher.  I gave it a 10 and I still think it should have been a ribbon winner.  You can feel the coarse texture of the fur, the grainy texture of the skin around rim of the eye and even the hair stuck on the eyeball makes me blink thinking about how that must feel.  I think you were robbed!', '2004-02-25 08:29:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(597592, 60288, 12253, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Hits: This is a well composed natural gradient photo.  The exposure looks about right.  Sharpness is good and there isn''t much noise.  The overall tones have fine aesthetics.<br/> <br/>Misses: Texture is downplayed here in the stone at this angle and with this light.  The granite looks is pretty smooth, so it''s really the engraving, the overall shape of the stone, and the clouds that represent surface texture here.  And the engraving is not even very visible here.<br/> <br/>Ideas. Perhaps another source of light from an assistant angled onto the stone would have brought out the engraving.  I think a perspective shift might have made it more dynamic as well: perhaps you could have captured the stone angling on the diagonal of the shot, with an even sharper perspective.  Or found a stone with a broken off area so an unsmoothed area of the granite were visible.<br/> <br/>Nice picture overall!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: Hits: This is a well composed natural gradient photo.  The exposure looks about right.  Sharpness is good and there isn''t much noise.  The overall tones have fine aesthetics. Misses: Texture is downplayed here in the stone at this angle and with this light.  The granite looks is pretty smooth, so it''s really the engraving, the overall shape of the stone, and the clouds that represent surface texture here.  And the engraving is not even very visible here. Ideas. Perhaps another source of light from an assistant angled onto the stone would have brought out the engraving.  I think a perspective shift might have made it more dynamic as well: perhaps you could have captured the stone angling on the diagonal of the shot, with an even sharper perspective.  Or found a stone with a broken off area so an unsmoothed area of the granite were visible. Nice picture overall!', '2004-02-25 08:45:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(597641, 61053, 16075, '<td valign="top">I''m very surprised this did not get a ribbon or place within the top 10 at least.  I gave it a 10.  It''s funny how people see things so differently.  When I look at this picture, I can feel the smooth polished wood, the sharp metal of the cross, the varying textures of the beads, and the tactile feel of the purse.  I can even feel the smooth cold glass of the store window in front of the mannequin which is evident due to the reflections.  I love the color and composition too.  This is still one of my favorites in this challenge.  I think you did an excellent job.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-25 09:16:47.</i></td>', 'I''m very surprised this did not get a ribbon or place within the top 10 at least.  I gave it a 10.  It''s funny how people see things so differently.  When I look at this picture, I can feel the smooth polished wood, the sharp metal of the cross, the varying textures of the beads, and the tactile feel of the purse.  I can even feel the smooth cold glass of the store window in front of the mannequin which is evident due to the reflections.  I love the color and composition too.  This is still one of my favorites in this challenge.  I think you did an excellent job.', '2004-02-25 09:16:19.000000', '2004-02-25 09:16:47.000000', 0),
