(598513, 60831, 15296, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and suggestions. I realize there isnt much here todo about textures. Ill try to stick to theme on next submission. Again, Thanks :)</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and suggestions. I realize there isnt much here todo about textures. Ill try to stick to theme on next submission. Again, Thanks :)', '2004-02-25 17:32:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(598543, 61116, 8860, '<td valign="top">Very crisp freshness coming through here. Good composition. <br/> <br/>Despite the overexposure, the dazzling sunlight actually enhances the the refractive nature of ice and is closer to realism.</td>', 'Very crisp freshness coming through here. Good composition.  Despite the overexposure, the dazzling sunlight actually enhances the the refractive nature of ice and is closer to realism.', '2004-02-25 17:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(598687, 60950, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very pretty colors with a nice texture to it.  Definately fits the challenge.  Nice use of limited dof.  <br/> <br/>I think all it needs is just a slight more sharpening to bring the textures out even more.  Overall it is a very pleasing image.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Very pretty colors with a nice texture to it.  Definately fits the challenge.  Nice use of limited dof.   I think all it needs is just a slight more sharpening to bring the textures out even more.  Overall it is a very pleasing image.   ', '2004-02-25 18:34:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(598706, 60768, 11793, '<td valign="top">nice photo</td>', 'nice photo', '2004-02-25 18:40:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(598926, 60921, 12151, '<td valign="top">Just to explain the small peak of lower scores for this photo, although it is technically good, I think others, like me, found the image as a whole unappealing.  In other words, I look at it and don''t think: "What a clean photo that shows off texture"; I think: "I would never want to eat this abnormally veined, gray cabbage, and I want better presentation of it" -- it''s a little unsettling.  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-25 21:10:21.</i></td>', 'Just to explain the small peak of lower scores for this photo, although it is technically good, I think others, like me, found the image as a whole unappealing.  In other words, I look at it and don''t think: "What a clean photo that shows off texture"; I think: "I would never want to eat this abnormally veined, gray cabbage, and I want better presentation of it" -- it''s a little unsettling.  ', '2004-02-25 21:04:56.000000', '2004-02-25 21:10:21.000000', 0),
(598940, 59916, 12151, '<td valign="top">I think you should have scored higher, although I''m not surprised that it didn''t.  Don''t be discouraged by the rankings - this photo has a lot of merit.  And any "imperfections" in the pattern you''ve captured really don''t matter to me because this is a photograph of a real environment - it definitely does not have a doctored "post-card" feel to it.  And at the same time you''ve got amazing fractal-like patterns in there.  It''s got the magic of reality rolled into a photo.</td>', 'I think you should have scored higher, although I''m not surprised that it didn''t.  Don''t be discouraged by the rankings - this photo has a lot of merit.  And any "imperfections" in the pattern you''ve captured really don''t matter to me because this is a photograph of a real environment - it definitely does not have a doctored "post-card" feel to it.  And at the same time you''ve got amazing fractal-like patterns in there.  It''s got the magic of reality rolled into a photo.', '2004-02-25 21:20:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(598959, 61057, 10644, '<td valign="top">wonderful detail and dof<br/>i think the background would be better if it had been a different color and provide more contrast.<br/>lovely composition and good feel of the texture and meeting the challenge</td>', 'wonderful detail and dofi think the background would be better if it had been a different color and provide more contrast.lovely composition and good feel of the texture and meeting the challenge', '2004-02-25 21:33:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(598981, 60932, 3724, '<td valign="top">Open Cap Mushroom is exemplary, but highest complements for your success... to review every picture of the challenge.  Every sentence is thoughtful!  A daunting task and hard work, but everyone who received your words was rewarded with insight and encouragement.  Each one is a fine model of an accomplished short critique writing style - worthy to study &amp; emulate.  Congratulations for your ribbon!</td>', 'Open Cap Mushroom is exemplary, but highest complements for your success... to review every picture of the challenge.  Every sentence is thoughtful!  A daunting task and hard work, but everyone who received your words was rewarded with insight and encouragement.  Each one is a fine model of an accomplished short critique writing style - worthy to study & emulate.  Congratulations for your ribbon!', '2004-02-25 21:45:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(599114, 60832, 806, '<td valign="top">wonderful portrait! this is what children''s portraits are all about. a bit more light on the face ... but an otherwise captivating image. :)</td>', 'wonderful portrait! this is what children''s portraits are all about. a bit more light on the face ... but an otherwise captivating image. :)', '2004-02-25 23:13:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(599157, 60896, 9581, '<td valign="top">Wow!! Didnt get to vote on this would of voted it high! Very simple yet shows more then that! It almost fits in the new challenge for this week also for silence!!</td>', 'Wow!! Didnt get to vote on this would of voted it high! Very simple yet shows more then that! It almost fits in the new challenge for this week also for silence!!', '2004-02-25 23:39:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(599369, 60921, 6870, '<td valign="top">Only we colorblind folks know how wonderful the tones of a nice b/w photo are, JJ, and this image certainly has them! I for one am now hungry!</td>', 'Only we colorblind folks know how wonderful the tones of a nice b/w photo are, JJ, and this image certainly has them! I for one am now hungry!', '2004-02-26 01:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(599524, 60780, 16004, '<td valign="top">Well, even though this shot was a rush job and I wasn''t very pleased with it, I am pleasantly surprised with how well it did and even more pleased with the encouraging and constructively critical comments left by the following lovely people.  And I learnt stuff, like:<br/> <br/>simplicity in titles is normally appreciated<br/>borders are generally not a good idea, especially when they''re a bit imposing like mine<br/>NeatImage totally destroys any texturey feel (though necessary because there was so much noise - still, hopefully extra practice will remedy this)<br/>and apparently, I''m not very original, dammit ;) ! (I''ll have to find the other chocolate one)<br/> <br/>Still, if anyone who left comments happens to find this, thanks!  I''m now very much inspired to perservere with this hobby / project.<br/> <br/>cheers<br/></td>', 'Well, even though this shot was a rush job and I wasn''t very pleased with it, I am pleasantly surprised with how well it did and even more pleased with the encouraging and constructively critical comments left by the following lovely people.  And I learnt stuff, like: simplicity in titles is normally appreciatedborders are generally not a good idea, especially when they''re a bit imposing like mineNeatImage totally destroys any texturey feel (though necessary because there was so much noise - still, hopefully extra practice will remedy this)and apparently, I''m not very original, dammit ;) ! (I''ll have to find the other chocolate one) Still, if anyone who left comments happens to find this, thanks!  I''m now very much inspired to perservere with this hobby / project. cheers', '2004-02-26 04:07:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(599603, 59895, 14614, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for my highest number of comments and highest scoring shot!  I really liked this photo and glad others shared my enjoyment.  The contradiction in the comments refect my trade-offs and conflicts when putting it together (border, b&amp;w, tonal quality, composition)  I get so excited when I see I''ve got a new comment and this challenge was quite exciting!<br/> <br/>I''ve gotten hooked on shooting flowers -- that could be a bad/good thing!</td>', 'Thanks to all for my highest number of comments and highest scoring shot!  I really liked this photo and glad others shared my enjoyment.  The contradiction in the comments refect my trade-offs and conflicts when putting it together (border, b&w, tonal quality, composition)  I get so excited when I see I''ve got a new comment and this challenge was quite exciting! I''ve gotten hooked on shooting flowers -- that could be a bad/good thing!', '2004-02-26 06:49:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(599851, 60840, 13728, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of your kind comments.  This shot was very easy to execute, but took many shots before I chose this one.  Basically the flower was against a black background and I used my 28-75 lens and a long exposure.  I set it to the final size and zoomed.  Sometimes I zoomed in and sometimes I zoomed out.  I used to do slides for multi projector shows with type and graphics in the "old Days" BC (before computers) and one of the effects we did with type was the zoom.  It looked cool with type and I have been playing with it on objects.  I have also seen it work really effectively in action shots also. Haven''t tried that yet myself.</td>', 'Thanks for all of your kind comments.  This shot was very easy to execute, but took many shots before I chose this one.  Basically the flower was against a black background and I used my 28-75 lens and a long exposure.  I set it to the final size and zoomed.  Sometimes I zoomed in and sometimes I zoomed out.  I used to do slides for multi projector shows with type and graphics in the "old Days" BC (before computers) and one of the effects we did with type was the zoom.  It looked cool with type and I have been playing with it on objects.  I have also seen it work really effectively in action shots also. Haven''t tried that yet myself.', '2004-02-26 11:23:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(599920, 59895, 772, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by admart01:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks to all for my highest number of comments and highest scoring shot!  I really liked this photo and glad others shared my enjoyment.  The contradiction in the comments refect my trade-offs and conflicts when putting it together (border, b&amp;w, tonal quality, composition)  I get so excited when I see I''ve got a new comment and this challenge was quite exciting!<br/> <br/>I''ve gotten hooked on shooting flowers -- that could be a bad/good thing! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I love photographing flowers, even though I haven''t done many.  I have a long list of specific flowers I want to photograph in the spring and summer though :)</td>', 'Originally posted by admart01: Thanks to all for my highest number of comments and highest scoring shot!  I really liked this photo and glad others shared my enjoyment.  The contradiction in the comments refect my trade-offs and conflicts when putting it together (border, b&w, tonal quality, composition)  I get so excited when I see I''ve got a new comment and this challenge was quite exciting! I''ve gotten hooked on shooting flowers -- that could be a bad/good thing!   I love photographing flowers, even though I haven''t done many.  I have a long list of specific flowers I want to photograph in the spring and summer though :)', '2004-02-26 11:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(599951, 60512, 15746, '<td valign="top">Ahh I wished this photo would place higher! I love this bug!</td>', 'Ahh I wished this photo would place higher! I love this bug!', '2004-02-26 13:00:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(600062, 61136, 16672, '<td valign="top">not sure what to say nice tree down boy! Maybe you should have been looking at a vagina instead of a tree since that is what it looks like.<br/></td>', 'not sure what to say nice tree down boy! Maybe you should have been looking at a vagina instead of a tree since that is what it looks like.', '2004-02-26 14:05:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(600117, 59916, 117, '<td valign="top">I just want people to view my images the prize doesn''t really matter to me? I gave along time ago here for some think a concept is better than the image. I''m just the opposite you have to show me the image and then I''ll worry about the concept and title last for after all it''s a digital photography contest. Thanks for everyone voting and commenting</td>', 'I just want people to view my images the prize doesn''t really matter to me? I gave along time ago here for some think a concept is better than the image. I''m just the opposite you have to show me the image and then I''ll worry about the concept and title last for after all it''s a digital photography contest. Thanks for everyone voting and commenting', '2004-02-26 14:38:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(600219, 59882, 17055, '<td valign="top">This is extra large bubble wrap that was at my work. I get a kick of the Out of Focus comments! I was looking for more of an artistic spin because I figured their might be some others using this as a textured piece.<br/> <br/>Thanks to all of you who voted on my first entry! Thanks for the comments also. Some were very helpful.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-27 11:00:05.</i></td>', 'This is extra large bubble wrap that was at my work. I get a kick of the Out of Focus comments! I was looking for more of an artistic spin because I figured their might be some others using this as a textured piece. Thanks to all of you who voted on my first entry! Thanks for the comments also. Some were very helpful.', '2004-02-26 16:07:04.000000', '2004-02-27 11:00:05.000000', 0),
