(601056, 60879, 2553, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to vote on (or even look at!) the texture challenge and I am so sorry!  This photo is wonderful, and I am so glad that you got a ribbon with it and it ended up on the home page where I could snap it up into my favorites folder!  Really lovely work, congratulations.</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to vote on (or even look at!) the texture challenge and I am so sorry!  This photo is wonderful, and I am so glad that you got a ribbon with it and it ended up on the home page where I could snap it up into my favorites folder!  Really lovely work, congratulations.', '2004-02-27 08:09:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(601120, 60832, 17203, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who commented! I knew the exposure and contrast on this could have been better, but I couldn''t exactly tell a tired 18 month old to hold the pose. The baby may compete with the texture, too (but the challenge was only to make the viewer <i>feel</i> texture). I certainly didn''t expect a top-10 finish, but what''s the deal with the 1 and 2 votes? Is Stevie Wonder participating?  ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-27 10:47:03.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all who commented! I knew the exposure and contrast on this could have been better, but I couldn''t exactly tell a tired 18 month old to hold the pose. The baby may compete with the texture, too (but the challenge was only to make the viewer feel texture). I certainly didn''t expect a top-10 finish, but what''s the deal with the 1 and 2 votes? Is Stevie Wonder participating?  ;-)', '2004-02-27 10:03:45.000000', '2004-02-27 10:47:03.000000', 0),
(601445, 59883, 16912, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments, I guess 4.2 is a decent starting point. If I get time I may retake the picture using your suggestions (focus is a pretty basic one lol). Looking forward to your comments in the fire challenge.</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments, I guess 4.2 is a decent starting point. If I get time I may retake the picture using your suggestions (focus is a pretty basic one lol). Looking forward to your comments in the fire challenge.', '2004-02-27 14:48:35.000000', NULL, 0),
